{"session_id":"svc-1779102591080887926","seq":0,"type":"session.start","ts":"2026-05-18T11:09:53.763119573Z","data":{"provider":"","model":"haiku","sticky":{"key_present":true,"assignment":"not_applicable","bonus":0},"utilization":{"observed_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z"},"resolved_harness":"claude","harness_source":"auto_route","resolved_model":"haiku","work_dir":"/var/tmp/ddx-exec-wt/.execute-bead-wt-fizeau-60ce39cb-20260518T110909-40651861","max_iterations":0,"prompt":"\u003cexecute-bead\u003e\n  \u003cinstructions\u003e\nYou are executing one bead in an isolated DDx execution worktree. The bead\u0026#39;s \u0026lt;description\u0026gt; and \u0026lt;acceptance\u0026gt; are the contract: every AC must be provably satisfied by a specific code, test, or file after your commit.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;## Step 0: size check\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;Too big if any holds:\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;- More than ~6 ACs spanning unrelated subsystems.\u0026#xA;- AC mixes design, implementation, integration tests, and docs.\u0026#xA;- Description names multiple feature-sized pieces.\u0026#xA;- More than ~500 lines across ~5+ files in unrelated packages.\u0026#xA;- If the bead description exceeds 8000 bytes, use a split-first pass.\u0026#xA;- Auto-decomposition is capped at depth 2: root beads may split once, children once more; reject third-level splits with an explanation.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;If too big, decompose:\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;1. `ddx bead create` for each child (copy parent\u0026#39;s labels and spec-id).\u0026#xA;2. `ddx bead dep add \u0026lt;child-id\u0026gt; \u0026lt;parent-id\u0026gt;` to record edges.\u0026#xA;3. `ddx bead update \u0026lt;parent-id\u0026gt; --notes \u0026#39;decomposed into \u0026lt;child-ids\u0026gt;\u0026#39;`.\u0026#xA;4. Write `no_changes_rationale.txt` under the bead metadata `bundle` path with child IDs, then stop.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;Decomposition alone is success. Do not mix it with implementation.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;## How to work\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;- Read first. If the bead names files, specs, or prior beads, read them before editing — do not guess.\u0026#xA;- Cross-reference each AC to concrete evidence (test, file, function) before committing. If you cannot point at it, it is not done.\u0026#xA;- Run the project\u0026#39;s test and lint commands before committing. **Do not commit red code** — fix failures first.\u0026#xA;- Run git/index mutations sequentially; do not use parallel tool calls for `git add`, `git commit`, or other staging/commit commands.\u0026#xA;- Stage with `git add \u0026lt;specific-paths\u0026gt;`; never `git add -A` (the worktree may have unrelated WIP).\u0026#xA;- If `lefthook run pre-commit` depends on staged files, rerun it after staging the exact commit set. A `no-staged-files` run is not acceptance evidence.\u0026#xA;- Commit exactly once when green; conventional-commit subject ending with `[\u0026lt;bead-id\u0026gt;]`. Stop after the commit.\u0026#xA;- Do not modify files outside the bead\u0026#39;s scope.\u0026#xA;- Current-bead lifecycle is orchestrator-owned. Do not run `ddx bead update \u0026lt;bead-id\u0026gt; --claim`, `ddx bead update \u0026lt;bead-id\u0026gt; --status \u0026lt;status\u0026gt;`, `ddx bead update \u0026lt;bead-id\u0026gt; --unclaim`, or `ddx bead close \u0026lt;bead-id\u0026gt;`. Step 0 still allows `ddx bead create`, `ddx bead dep add`, and `ddx bead update \u0026lt;parent-id\u0026gt; --notes \u0026#39;decomposed into \u0026lt;child-ids\u0026gt;\u0026#39;`.\u0026#xA;- If you cannot finish, write `no_changes_rationale.txt` under the bead metadata `bundle` path before exiting. No commit or rationale ⇒ DDx records `no_evidence_produced`.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;## no_changes contract\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;The `no_changes_rationale.txt` file under the bead metadata `bundle` path must contain one of:\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;- `verification_command: \u0026lt;cmd\u0026gt;` — repo cwd; exit 0 closes, nonzero rejects.\u0026#xA;- `status: open` + `reason: \u0026lt;retryable\u0026gt;` — open, smart retry.\u0026#xA;- `status: proposed` + `reason: \u0026lt;operator needed\u0026gt;` — operator lane.\u0026#xA;- `status: blocked` + `reason: \u0026lt;external blocker\u0026gt;` — blocked lane.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;No pseudo-statuses. Bare rationales and `status: needs_investigation` are rejected.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;For orchestrator decomposition, add `orchestrator_action: decompose` alongside `status: open`.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;## Reports\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;Reports go under the bead metadata `bundle` path in `.ddx/executions/`. **Never write reports to `/tmp` or outside the repo**. Use a named in-repo path when given; otherwise write `\u0026lt;short-name\u0026gt;.md` there. Commit it with the code.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;## Mode and overrides\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;DDX_MODE=bead_execution: edit code/docs for bead AC. Only broad queue-steward default is overridden; tracker, merge-policy, verification, safety stay active. Bead description/AC override CLAUDE.md, AGENTS.md, and defaults.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;## Review gate\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;- The review is a gate, not an escape hatch — meet every AC in this pass.\u0026#xA;- Address every BLOCKING `\u0026lt;review-findings\u0026gt;` item; do not declare `no_changes` with blocking findings open.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;## Constraints\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;- Work only inside this execution worktree.\u0026#xA;- Keep `.ddx/executions/` intact — DDx uses it as execution evidence.\u0026#xA;- **Never run `ddx init`** — the workspace is initialized.\u0026#xA;- Do not modify files outside the bead\u0026#39;s named scope.\u0026#xA;- Do not rewrite CLAUDE.md, AGENTS.md, or other instruction files unless the bead asks.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;## When the work is done\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;After the commit succeeds and every AC is verified, stop. Return control to the orchestrator.\n  \u003c/instructions\u003e\n  \u003cbead id=\"fizeau-60ce39cb\"\u003e\n    \u003ctitle\u003eclaude-tui: implement Harness+Account+Quota turn execution over internal/pty with intermediate ProgressEvents\u003c/title\u003e\n    \u003cdescription\u003e\nPROBLEM: The claude-tui skeleton from child #1 has no real turn-execution path. ADR-013 §3 requires that claude-tui drive the Anthropic CLI through internal/pty/ and emit intermediate tool_call/tool_result ProgressEvents DURING the turn (not at Stop), via PreToolUse/PostToolUse hooks. Subscription billing is observed off the live CLI session, so the wire format must be the interactive PTY surface.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;ROOT CAUSE:\u0026#xA;- The existing claude harness uses --print and only emits a Final ProgressEvent on subprocess termination; ADR-013 mandates mid-turn events for claude-tui.\u0026#xA;- internal/pty/ exists but is not driven by any harness yet; session-pool, /clear-between-turns, and orphan-reaper concerns from ADR-013 are unimplemented for this harness.\u0026#xA;- AccountHarness and QuotaHarness need CLI-observed signals (identity, usage) instead of API-metered numbers; existing helpers live in the neutral anthropic/ package after child #1.\u0026#xA;- Per testing concern in ADR-013, loop overhead beyond inference must stay under 10ms and wall-time-per-turn must stay within 2x of claude --print on equivalent prompts.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;PROPOSED FIX:\u0026#xA;1. Implement claudetui.Harness.RunTurn: open or reuse an internal/pty/ session, write the prompt, drive readers, terminate on the CLI\u0026#39;s end-of-turn marker, return Final event.\u0026#xA;2. Install PreToolUse/PostToolUse hook handlers that emit tool_call and tool_result ProgressEvents on the harness event channel as they fire mid-turn.\u0026#xA;3. Implement a session pool keyed by working directory: between turns issue /clear; on shutdown reap any orphaned PTY processes.\u0026#xA;4. Resolve hook-conflict concern from ADR-013 by routing claude-tui\u0026#39;s hooks through the existing conflict-arbitration layer (no new mechanism).\u0026#xA;5. Implement AccountHarness.Identity off CLI auth status output (parsed via anthropic/ helpers).\u0026#xA;6. Implement QuotaHarness.Quota off CLI quota observation surface (parsed via anthropic/ helpers).\u0026#xA;7. Add a benchmark that compares per-turn wall time against a claude --print baseline on a shared canned prompt and asserts the ratchet.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;NON-SCOPE:\u0026#xA;- ModelDiscoveryHarness implementation and no-static-fallback enforcement (child #3).\u0026#xA;- Capability baseline rows, evidence IDs, ADR-013 status promotion (child #4).\u0026#xA;- Cassette-driven static fallback for production code (forbidden by fizeau-89eca738).\u0026#xA;- Service-side changes beyond what child #1 already wired.\u0026#xA;- Redesigning the hook-conflict arbitration layer; reuse existing infrastructure.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;Depends on child #1. Governing artifacts: ADR-013 §3, CONTRACT-004, internal/pty/ library.\n    \u003c/description\u003e\n    \u003cacceptance\u003e\n1) TestClaudeTuiTurnEmitsIntermediateToolEvents asserts that for a prompt that triggers a tool use, the harness event channel yields at least one tool_call ProgressEvent before the Final event, and that every tool_call is followed by a matching tool_result.\u0026#xA;2) TestClaudeTuiSessionPoolReusesAndClears asserts /clear is issued between consecutive turns sharing a working directory and that the underlying PTY session is reused (same pid).\u0026#xA;3) TestClaudeTuiOrphanReaper asserts that on harness shutdown any leftover PTY child processes are reaped within a bounded timeout.\u0026#xA;4) TestClaudeTuiHookConflictRouting asserts claude-tui\u0026#39;s PreToolUse/PostToolUse hooks register through the shared conflict-arbitration layer and coexist with user-defined hooks without duplication.\u0026#xA;5) TestClaudeTuiAccountIdentity asserts AccountHarness.Identity() returns the CLI-observed account string parsed via internal/harnesses/anthropic helpers.\u0026#xA;6) TestClaudeTuiQuotaObservation asserts QuotaHarness.Quota() returns CLI-observed usage parsed via internal/harnesses/anthropic helpers.\u0026#xA;7) BenchmarkClaudeTuiTurnWallTime asserts mean wall-time-per-turn is within 2x of the claude --print baseline on the shared canned prompt, and that loop overhead beyond inference is under 10ms.\u0026#xA;8) go test ./... -count=1 is green.\u0026#xA;9) lefthook run pre-commit is green.\n    \u003c/acceptance\u003e\n    \u003clabels\u003ehelix, phase:build, kind:feature, area:harness, harness:claude-tui, spec:ADR-013\u003c/labels\u003e\n    \u003cmetadata parent=\"fizeau-9b3b85df\" base-rev=\"d3919bac833fad2c3deb7fa77a33f8c75f26b3b6\" bundle=\".ddx/executions/20260518T110909-40651861\"/\u003e\n  \u003c/bead\u003e\n  \u003cgoverning\u003e\n    \u003cnote\u003eNo governing references were pre-resolved. The bead description above is the primary contract. If it names files, specs, or prior beads, read them first. Ground decisions in repository state; do not guess.\u003c/note\u003e\n  \u003c/governing\u003e\n\u003c/execute-bead\u003e\n","metadata":{"DDX_MODE":"bead_execution","GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL":"/var/tmp/ddx-exec-wt/.execute-bead-wt-fizeau-60ce39cb-20260518T110909-40651861/.ddx/executions/20260518T110909-40651861/embedded/git-global.cfg","GIT_CONFIG_SYSTEM":"/dev/null","PATH":"/var/tmp/ddx-exec-wt/.execute-bead-wt-fizeau-60ce39cb-20260518T110909-40651861/.ddx/executions/20260518T110909-40651861/embedded/git-bin:/usr/local/cuda/bin:/home/erik/.jbang/bin:/home/erik/.opencode/bin:/home/erik/.local/share/mise/installs/bun/1.3.11/bin:/home/erik/.local/share/mise/installs/node/22.21.1/bin:/Users/erik/.antigravity/antigravity/bin:/home/erik/bin:/home/erik/.local/share/mise/shims:/home/linuxbrew/.linuxbrew/bin:/home/linuxbrew/.linuxbrew/sbin:/home/erik/.local/bin:/home/erik/bin:/home/erik/.dotfiles/git-subrepo/lib:/home/linuxbrew/.linuxbrew/bin:/home/linuxbrew/.linuxbrew/sbin:/Applications/SnowSQL.app/Contents/MacOS:/home/linuxbrew/.linuxbrew/bin:/home/linuxbrew/.linuxbrew/sbin:/Users/erik/.antigravity/antigravity/bin:/home/erik/bin:/home/erik/.loca